Integer multipart field names are now strings before they reach urllib3, so `prepare()` no longer raises `AttributeError` on keys like `1`.

`Request._encode_files` in `src/requests/models.py` coerces every multipart field name with `str()` (bytes names are still decoded as UTF-8). An int key becomes the field name `"1"`. File-tuple shapes and the urlencoded path are unchanged: `data={1: "a"}` with no files still prepares the body `1=a`.

`test_nonstring_multipart_field_names` in `tests/test_requests.py` calls `prepare()` with no network connection and covers an int key in `data` when `files` is set, an int key in `files`, and the urlencoded body.

